### Density Limits and Interest Penalties
Balance accumulation is regulated by two land-density thresholds:
 * The soft limit (optimal capacity) sits at S_p = 100 \times L_p. Below this threshold, entities receive full interest. When balance exceeds S_p, the HUD balance text turns red to warn the player of diminishing returns.
 * The hard limit (maximum capacity) sits at H_p = 150 \times L_p. Balance cannot exceed this ceiling under any circumstances.
When balance is between S_p and H_p, the effective interest rate decays linearly toward zero:
