Annexing neutral pixels consumes deployed troops from the active expansion pool. Conquering one neutral pixel requires approximately 1 to 2\text{ troops} under normal conditions. If the deployed force runs out before the selected territory is fully annexed, expansion halts at the current perimeter. Any unspent troops remaining in the expansion pool once forward movement stops are refunded to the entity's main balance.
Frontline expansion does not occur instantly across the map. Instead, new pixels are claimed in successive geometric waves whose propagation rate depends on the entity's total land area.
