## Combat Resolution, Structural Defense, and Attrition Mechanics
Combat between competing entities resolves through deterministic mathematical attrition along active borders. The system includes a built-in advantage for defenders: defending troops absorb damage twice as efficiently as attacking troops.
```
Attacker: Deploys attacking force (A) and pays 1.171875% tax
    ├── Combat Exchange: Clamped troop attrition ratio (0.6 to 2.0 window)
    ├── Defender Advantage: Defending units inflict casualties at 2:1 structural efficiency
    └── Territorial Breaches: Pixels transfer to attacker if defender's balance is depleted

```
