Conversely, the attacking force suffers casualties at double that rate when engaging a fortified enemy position. Because of this 2:1 defender advantage, attacking an opponent of equal size with more than 10% to 20% of one's balance causes heavy troop losses, leaving the attacker vulnerable to counterattacks from other neighbors.
